    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0197" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg191"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith copy of a note<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d206-f1"/> which I have this day addressed to the British
                    ambassador at this capital, suggesting that the time has arrived for the
                    Governments of the United States and Great Britain to cooperate in securing the
                    adhesion of other powers, especially Russia and Japan, to the award of the Paris
                    Tribunal.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
